# 2026-10-26 10:44:25.594259
+Use the ELM requirements below as the baseline for reviewing the existing Phase-1 implementation. Do not regenerate the project.
+
+Key requirements from the specification:
+- Leave categories: CL, RH, SCL, EL, COL, VL.
+- CL: 8 days/year; half-day CL supported; no carry-forward.
+- RH: 2 days/year, must match the currently effective published RH calendar.
+- SCL: up to 15 days/year; no carry-forward.
+- EL: 30 days/year for non-faculty; unused EL carries forward.
+- VL: 60 days/year for faculty, only during academic-calendar vacation periods; unused VL converts to EL at 2:1 at year-end, including fractional conversion.
+- COL: 20 days/year for eligible employees; unused COL carries forward.
+- EL/COL/VL count continuously across intervals, including weekends and closed holidays; this rule does not apply to CL/SCL/RH.
+- Applications validate eligibility, balances, calendars, overlaps, and half-day CL exceptions.
+- Substitute must be another employee, not the applicant, with no overlapping pending/approved leave; required consent must be accepted before approval routing continues.
+- CL/RH are finally decided by the Unit Head.
+- SCL/EL/COL/VL require Unit Head recommendation, then the configured higher-sanction path.
+- Pending withdrawal terminates all further processing. Approved-leave cancellation before start follows the original hierarchy and restores deducted balance if approved.
+- Extensions and resumptions are supported for EL/COL/VL.
+
+Inspect the source files now available in context. Compare implementation with these requirements and the extracted specifications if accessible. Report only evidence-based bugs or missing tests, with exact file paths, severity, and regression tests. If a requirement cannot be verified from the files in context, say so and request only the specific missing files. Do not edit code yet.
+
+Do not assume a bug merely because a requirement is not implemented in the few files shown; inspect relevant services/models/tests before concluding.
